diff --git a/docs/plugins/sqlite-private-recovery.md b/docs/plugins/sqlite-private-recovery.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..771d58a63c6f417649e03c8ae0745dbfbcdc7c35
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/plugins/sqlite-private-recovery.md
@@ -0,0 +1,40 @@
+---
+summary: "Source-owned private logical capture through the original SQLite worker actor and lease"
+title: "Private SQLite recovery admission"
+---
+
+The SQLite runtime SDK can bind an opaque recovery target to an existing native
+store and its original logical connection. Binding grants no private permission.
+Ordinary tool, Gateway, card, read/write and database admissions cannot invoke
+the reserved `private-recovery.capture` operation.
+
+`bindSqliteWorkerRecoveryTarget(store, connection, assertConnectionCurrent, decode)`
+captures the original admitted actor and lease. Its callback must describe that
+original connection lifecycle, not reopen a pathname or adopt a replacement.
+`capturePrivateSqliteWorkerRecovery(target, authority, operationId)` requires a
+live opaque host-issued private authority bound to that exact target. The
+host-only issuer is not exported through the SDK. Neither JSON nor matching IDs
+can construct the authority. The runtime client validates the serialized command
+against its registered source-owned private factory before dispatch.
+
+The backend requests prepare, transaction and precommit admission using the
+retained private operation port. Source checks can revoke permission across
+awaits or during a callback. Capture uses the original worker-held database
+handle; snapshot reconstruction and semantic verification remain on that worker.
+The existing actor operation stays retained through descriptor custody and its
+durable acknowledgement. Unknown acknowledgements are not replayed.
+
+Workboard supplies the codec for its unchanged schema3 and complete raw logical
+contents, including claims, history and blobs. Capturing them does not rearm
+claims or start work. Its worker result is bounded to 32 MiB; descriptor custody
+may impose a smaller quota and fails without truncation. Host code performs
+transport and manifest checks only; it does not open SQLite on the Gateway main
+thread. Inert restore stays independent of the operational store initializer,
+startup, migration, notifications and dispatch.
+
+This source feature has no default private issuer, route or schedule. A release
+integrator must bind the trusted startup/private owner and executed SDK/worker
+images, verify the shared authority registry, and admit an exact private custodian.
+Doctor, CLI and ordinary startup acquire no private capture authority. The
+isolated overlay's synthetic unit receipts do not establish those operational
+facts or permission to capture real user data.
